{"content":[{"c":["JESHANAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Border city in the hill country of Ephraim that King Abijah of Judah (913–910 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},") seized from King Jeroboam I (930–909 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},") and the northern kingdom during a civil war (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.13.19","r":"2Chr.13.19","rawR":"2Chr.13.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.13.19","value":"2Chr.13.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 13:19"},"). The Greek and Syriac reading of “Jeshanah” as one of the towns between which Samuel erected the Ebenezer stone may be preferred to the Hebrew “Shen” in ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.7.12","r":"1Sam.7.12","rawR":"1Sam.7.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.7.12","value":"1Sam.7.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Samuel 7:12"},". Its location is perhaps near Burj el-Isaneh, four miles (6.4 kilometers) north of Bethel."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Jeshanah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Chr 13:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.13.19","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.13.19","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.13.19"},{"anchorText":"1 Samuel 7:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.7.12","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.7.12","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.7.12"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"188b4248e3d20247c854b1d3cfe2fc8f44231ee0bf551cf63be440ab72eb96f1","sourceItemName":"Jeshanah","sourceItemOrder":207,"sourceMember":"Articles/J.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Jeshanah","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Jeshanah","title":"Jeshanah","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}